# evidence-for: US-004, FR-013, FR-015, FR-035, AC-015, AC-016, AC-017
#
# US-004. The page names `iPhone`, `PostgreSQL` and `GraphQL` on the first
# runs below and is never reported for any of them: the static IDENT_ALLOW
# compares lowercased and carries the real spellings (AC-015 / FR-015).
#
# FR-013 names exactly three allowlist sources -- labels, screens.name and
# commands -- and the first line of output is the tuple the loader iterates,
# which is all three and only those three. The survey carries a screen with a
# name and a screen with only a path: the named screen excuses `DataSources`
# (its spaced name reaches the lens with the whitespace removed, the same
# source in a second spelling), and the path-only screen excuses nothing, so
# the page naming its file stem `DataSourcesPage` is still reported.
#
# The auditLog run is CT-003's "case-insensitively" made visible (D-096): the
# survey spells the screen `auditLog` and the page writes `AuditLog`, two
# spellings CODE_IDENT reports separately, and they meet only because both
# sides are lowercased before the compare. An all-lowercase `auditlog` -- which
# the test comment here used to name -- matches no branch of CODE_IDENT and is
# never reported at all, so it could not have shown this.
#
# The two header lines after it are the FR-035 count against surveys of two
# different sizes (D-095): two labels print 2, five print 5. One fixture cannot
# tell a real count from a constant.
#
# The two unreadable-survey runs report the label again and say so in the
# header line rather than crashing; the last line counts the tracebacks on
# stderr: zero.

